guide.Add("DCSync|domains",new string[]{"This is a replication capability candidate on one domain, supported by paired grants or an explicit source observation.","Verify both replication rights on this domain, each grant trustee, membership witnesses and full-token deny behavior.","Remove or narrow the unauthorized prerequisite grant or membership at its actual source; preserve approved replication services.","Rescan both grants and all relevant memberships. Confirm the candidate and alternative routes are absent while approved replication remains healthy.","Do not remove required domain-controller or synchronization permissions. Changing a shared group can affect other delegated services."});
guide.Add("GenericAll|domains",new string[]{"Control of the domain-root object or its permission list can affect domain-wide delegation and needs review at the domain boundary.","Verify the effective object-control grant and review replication permissions separately, including trustees, group paths and denies.","Narrow unauthorized domain-root full control or permission-management delegation while preserving approved directory-service roles.","Rescan the domain-root ACL and replication prerequisites, check alternative grants, and confirm directory services remain healthy.","Domain-root permission changes can disrupt replication and delegated services; preserve the original ACL and approved service grants."});
guide.Add("WriteDacl|domains",new string[]{"Control of the domain-root object or its permission list can affect domain-wide delegation and needs review at the domain boundary.","Verify the effective object-control grant and review replication permissions separately, including trustees, group paths and denies.","Narrow unauthorized domain-root full control or permission-management delegation while preserving approved directory-service roles.","Rescan the domain-root ACL and replication prerequisites, check alternative grants, and confirm directory services remain healthy.","Domain-root permission changes can disrupt replication and delegated services; preserve the original ACL and approved service grants."});
guide.Add("CanRDP|computers",new string[]{"The relationship represents potential Remote Desktop access; it does not establish local-administrator access or privileged execution.","Check Remote Desktop authorization, logon allow and deny policy, service availability, firewall reachability and authentication requirements.","Remove unnecessary Remote Desktop authorization at the responsible local-group or policy assignment.","Rescan the assignment and validate allowed support access using the approved endpoint-management process.","Removing a shared remote-support assignment can lock out legitimate operators."});
guide.Add("HasSession|users",new string[]{"The target user had a recorded session on the source computer. This is time-sensitive evidence, not a reusable permission grant.","Check when the session was observed and whether it is still active. A session does not prove credentials remain available.","Coordinate ending an unneeded privileged session and separate privileged administration from lower-trust hosts.","Collect comparable session data again and verify the approved administration workflow; a single absent session does not prove a lasting fix.","Signing out a user can interrupt work. Session observations can change without any permission change."});
guide.Add("WriteGPLink|ous",new string[]{"Editing policy links can alter policy scope, but the effect depends on the linked policy and which users or computers actually receive it.","Verify linked GPO control, filtering, enforcement, inheritance and the affected objects; site scope also depends on site and subnet configuration.","Restrict link editing to the approved policy-management role and remove unauthorized links only after reviewing their scope.","Review the remaining links and validate effective policy on representative affected users or computers.","Changing a link can remove legitimate security or service settings across an entire policy scope."});
guide.Add("WriteGPLink|domains",new string[]{"Editing policy links can alter policy scope, but the effect depends on the linked policy and which users or computers actually receive it.","Verify linked GPO control, filtering, enforcement, inheritance and the affected objects; site scope also depends on site and subnet configuration.","Restrict link editing to the approved policy-management role and remove unauthorized links only after reviewing their scope.","Review the remaining links and validate effective policy on representative affected users or computers.","Changing a link can remove legitimate security or service settings across an entire policy scope."});
guide.Add("WriteGPLink|sites",new string[]{"Editing policy links can alter policy scope, but the effect depends on the linked policy and which users or computers actually receive it.","Verify linked GPO control, filtering, enforcement, inheritance and the affected objects; site scope also depends on site and subnet configuration.","Restrict link editing to the approved policy-management role and remove unauthorized links only after reviewing their scope.","Review the remaining links and validate effective policy on representative affected users or computers.","Changing a link can remove legitimate security or service settings across an entire policy scope."});
guide.Add("WriteAccountRestrictions|users",new string[]{"This records a property-set write grant. The attributes and account-control changes permitted in practice depend on target type and directory checks.","Inspect the property-set members and additional rights required for each proposed account or delegation change.","Delegate only the individual account-restriction attributes required by the approved provisioning workflow.","Rescan the exact attribute permissions and test the intended provisioning workflow without changing unrelated account controls.","Do not infer account takeover or replace all account-control settings from this observation alone."});
guide.Add("WriteAccountRestrictions|computers",new string[]{"This records a property-set write grant. The attributes and account-control changes permitted in practice depend on target type and directory checks.","Inspect the property-set members and additional rights required for each proposed account or delegation change.","Delegate only the individual account-restriction attributes required by the approved provisioning workflow.","Rescan the exact attribute permissions and test the intended provisioning workflow without changing unrelated account controls.","Do not infer account takeover or replace all account-control settings from this observation alone."});
guide.Add("ADCSESC1|domains",new string[]{"An enrollment capability candidate reaches this domain through imported template and CA evidence.","Validate the same principal/token on both enrollment branches, the exact publishing CA, direct-root and NTAuth trust, host state and current authentication enforcement.","Review whether requester-supplied identities are required, narrow unauthorized enrollment grants, and consider approval or signature controls that preserve legitimate enrollment.","Rescan the template and CA service permissions and trust data. Confirm the candidate is removed and approved certificate enrollment and renewal still work.","CA/template changes can disrupt authentication, auto-enrollment and renewal; preserve the original configuration and coordinate with the PKI owner."});
guide.Add("AdminTo|computers",new string[]{"A local administrator assignment can permit broad changes on the endpoint when effective authorization and remote/local access conditions allow it.","Validate current local/policy group membership, nested groups, token filtering, logon policy and the actual supported access method.","Remove only the unnecessary local-administrator assignment at its real source, preserving approved device-management access.","Rescan local and policy-derived groups, test intended management access and check alternative privileged assignments.","Changing a shared administrator assignment can lock out support or service management."});
guide.Add("CanPSRemote|computers",new string[]{"This is potential remote-management authorization on a computer, separate from verified privileged execution.","Check the exact protocol/application endpoint authorization, service state, firewall path and authentication restrictions.","Narrow unnecessary remote-management assignments at the local group, policy or application authorization that supplies them.","Recollect the assignment and test the approved management workflow through its intended endpoint.","Removing a shared remoting assignment can disrupt legitimate operations even when no administrator capability was established."});
